# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings.
#
# This repository is checked out on an NTFS mount with core.autocrlf=true,
# which rewrites text files to CRLF in the working tree. Windows tools do not
# care. Bash does: a sourced script whose lines end in \r appends a carriage
# return to every value it exports, so
#
#     export MRA_LEAN_PROJECT=/home/.../mathlib_playground
#
# becomes a path ending in \r that no directory matches, and
#
#     export MRA_MODEL=google_genai:gemini-3.8-flash
#
# becomes a model name no provider recognises. It also breaks `if` blocks
# outright, which is how `source scripts/env.sh` came to print seven
# "command not found" lines and a syntax error, and silently skipped loading
# ~/.mra-secrets -- making a correctly-installed key look absent.
#
# Diagnosed the hard way: three FATAL rows in check_install.py, all one cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
